  "interpretation": [
    "Slow response reads expire for both previous and final clients (about12.02/12.35seconds here). The previous write remains alive at3.51seconds until the owned peer closes; the final write returns a deadline error at2.02seconds despite19progress events. No full request LF reaches the synthetic peer. All exact owned clients are reaped and sockets removed. No real server mutation or native/model execution is involved.",
    "The healthy4MiBreply costs16.57% and16.85% more elapsed RPC time in two paired repeats:about6.6ms to7.7ms. This is an accepted security cost,not a performance gain. Empty replies vary+10.2%/-34.5%; no repeatable small-request gain or regression is attributed. All exact full reply and state hashes match.",
    "These budgets bound established-connection wire I/O; they do not bound connection setup,CPU/mutex handling,filesystem operations,stdout consumers or native commands. OS scheduling can delay observation; no hard real-time guarantee. Same-user control remains trusted and powerful.",
    "New slow-peer probes are Unix-only. Windows local compilation and ordinary cross-platformCI do not establish equivalent dynamic slow-peer timing. No sandbox,exactly-once mutation,arbitrary Bash compatibility or production-completeness claim."
  ],
